From: LuneOS
Subject: [PATCH] NotificationService: tell subscribers when a toast is closed

cb_closeToast() deletes the row from History and nothing else. It never posts
on the getToastNotification subscription, so every subscriber keeps its own
copy of the toast: the call answers {"returnValue":true} while the banner
stays on screen and its entry stays in the notification area. An application
that posts a banner and later withdraws it cannot make it go away.

closeAlert() already does this properly - it builds an alertAction "close"
message carrying alertInfo.timestamp and posts it, and the shell's alert model
switches on that action to remove the matching row. Toasts have the same
shape (createToast puts a timestamp and a sourceId into the payload) and had
no equivalent, so mirror it: "close" carries toastInfo.timestamp for the
single-toast case, "closeAll" carries toastInfo.sourceId for the bulk case.

Posted with persistentMsg and staleMsg false, so the close is delivered
without being written back into History.

The consumer side needs the matching change in luna-surfacemanager-base,
whose toast model has no removal branch today.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]

--- a/src/NotificationService.cpp
+++ b/src/NotificationService.cpp
@@ -1888,6 +1888,8 @@
     std::string timestamp;
 
     pbnjson::JValue request;
+    pbnjson::JValue postToastMessage;
+    pbnjson::JValue toastInfo;
     JUtil::Error error;
 
     request = JUtil::parse(LSMessageGetPayload(msg), "closeToast", &error);
@@ -1919,6 +1921,17 @@
         }
 
         History::instance()->deleteMessage("timestamp", timestamp);
+
+        // Deleting the history row is not enough: subscribers hold their own
+        // copy of the toast and are never told it went away, so the banner
+        // stays on screen. Post a close the same way closeAlert does.
+        postToastMessage = pbnjson::Object();
+        toastInfo = pbnjson::Object();
+        toastInfo.put("timestamp", timestamp);
+        postToastMessage.put("toastAction", "close");
+        postToastMessage.put("toastInfo", toastInfo);
+
+        NotificationService::instance()->postToastNotification(postToastMessage, false, false, errText);
     }
     else if (!sourceId.empty())
     {
@@ -1948,6 +1961,14 @@
         }
 
         History::instance()->deleteMessage("sourceId", sourceId);
+
+        postToastMessage = pbnjson::Object();
+        toastInfo = pbnjson::Object();
+        toastInfo.put("sourceId", sourceId);
+        postToastMessage.put("toastAction", "closeAll");
+        postToastMessage.put("toastInfo", toastInfo);
+
+        NotificationService::instance()->postToastNotification(postToastMessage, false, false, errText);
     }
 
     success = true;
